+// The server environment (nsd's environment id: "lp1" live, "dd1" development, "sd1" / "sp1" / "dp1" the other server sets). In nnSdk-16_2_3
+// nn::oe::GetServerEnvironmentType does not answer itself: it tail-calls nn::nsd::GetApplicationServerEnvironmentType (sdk+0x394670), which connects to
+// the nsd service (nsd:u, then nsd:a) and aborts with Result 0xe8d when the connection fails (sdk+0x395d28) instead of returning a failure. The host
+// serves neither service, and Hogwarts Legacy asks at boot (main+0x17c4c44, where Unreal builds its environment id): it aborted there. A retail console
+// is the live environment: 1, which this game maps to "lp1" (its jump table at main+0x62027e1: 0 "dd1", 1 "lp1", 2 "sd1", 3 "sp1", 4 "dp1"), the id
+// nn::nsd::GetEnvironmentIdentifier answers with (hle_offline.c)
+HLE_FORCE("_ZN2nn2oe24GetServerEnvironmentTypeEv", "server environment: retail (nsd:u is not served and the SDK aborts when it cannot connect)", int, h_oe_ServerEnv, void) { return 1; }
+
